sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer as PER-001 (Customer)
    participant Channel as Mobile App / Web Portal<br/>(Channel)
    participant PayOpsAPI as CAP-003<br/>Payment Operations API
    participant EventBus as SVC-102<br/>Event Bus
    participant RetailAPI as CAP-001<br/>Retail Banking API
    participant Notifications as SVC-053<br/>Notification Service
    participant Audit as SVC-103<br/>Audit & Logging
    participant BACS as BACS / Vocalink<br/>(External Scheme)

    Note over Customer,BACS: Pre-condition: £87.50 collected by BRITISH GAS on 15 May 2026<br/>Customer believes collection was taken in error

    Note over Customer,BACS: PH-051 — Indemnity Claim under Direct Debit Guarantee

    Customer->>Channel: Navigate to Direct Debits → BRITISH GAS → £87.50 (15 May 2026) → Dispute this payment
    Channel-->>Customer: Display DD Guarantee: "You are entitled to a full and immediate refund of £87.50.<br/>No reason required." Options: [Claim Refund] [✓ Cancel mandate]

    Customer->>Channel: Confirm claim: reason='Amount taken was incorrect', mandate_cancel=true

    Channel->>PayOpsAPI: POST /payments/v1/direct-debits/{ddi_id}/indemnity-claim<br/>{collection_id, claimed_amount: 87.50, claim_reason: '...', mandate_cancel_requested: true}
    Note right of PayOpsAPI: SVC-009 validates claim against ENT-035.<br/>Creates indemnity claim record.<br/>Updates ENT-035.status = indemnity_claimed.

    PayOpsAPI-->>Channel: 202 Accepted {claim_id, claimed_amount: 87.50,<br/>credit_sla: "Within 30 seconds — DD Guarantee",<br/>mandate_cancellation_status: cancellation_initiated}

    PayOpsAPI->>EventBus: Publish DirectDebitIndemnityClaimFiled (EVT-074)<br/>{claim_id, collection_id, ddi_id, account_id, claimed_amount: 87.50, mandate_cancel_requested: true}
    Note right of EventBus: CRITICAL cross-capability event.<br/>CAP-003 → CAP-001 boundary.<br/>30-second SLA on SVC-001 consumer.

    EventBus->>Audit: Write EVT-074 to WORM audit log IMMEDIATELY<br/>(Consumer Duty + DD Guarantee evidence — before any downstream processing)

    Channel-->>Customer: "Your claim has been submitted. £87.50 will be credited<br/>within 30 seconds. Your Direct Debit has been cancelled."

    Note over EventBus,RetailAPI: ⚡ CRITICAL: DD Guarantee immediate credit obligation — < 30 seconds

    EventBus->>RetailAPI: Consume EVT-074 (HIGH-PRIORITY consumer group)<br/>→ credit account £87.50 immediately. Idempotent on claim_id.
    Note right of RetailAPI: SVC-001 credits account ledger £87.50.<br/>DD Guarantee: unconditional, no investigation before credit.

    RetailAPI->>EventBus: Publish AccountCredited {account_id, amount: 87.50,<br/>credit_type: dd_indemnity, claim_id, credited_at: 2026-04-15T10:30:18Z}
    Note left of RetailAPI: Total elapsed from EVT-074: < 30 seconds ✓

    EventBus->>PayOpsAPI: Consume AccountCredited → confirm credit processed<br/>→ initiate BACS recovery and mandate cancellation

    par BACS indemnity recovery from originator
        PayOpsAPI->>BACS: Submit BACS Indemnity Claim: recover £87.50 from originator SUN 123456 (BRITISH GAS)
        Note right of BACS: Originator is liable under BACS scheme.<br/>Bank recovers after crediting customer.
    and Mandate cancellation (AUDDIS 0C)
        PayOpsAPI->>BACS: Submit AUDDIS 0C: cancel DDI SUN 123456, ref BGS-001234567
        Note right of BACS: ENT-034.status = cancelled.<br/>Future collections from this originator will not be honoured.
    end

    par Customer notification
        EventBus->>Notifications: Consume AccountCredited → send indemnity confirmation
        Notifications-->>Customer: Push + email: "£87.50 credited under Direct Debit Guarantee.<br/>Direct Debit with BRITISH GAS cancelled.<br/>BACS claim ref: BACS-IND-2026-04-15-001."
    and Audit trail
        EventBus->>Audit: Write AccountCredited to WORM audit log<br/>(7-year retention — Consumer Duty complaint evidence)
    end

    Note over Customer,BACS: Outcome: Customer credited £87.50 ✓ | Mandate cancelled ✓<br/>BACS recovery from originator initiated ✓ | Full audit trail recorded ✓
